# IDE
.vscode/
.idea/
.claude/
*.swp
*.swo

# ── Android app — laptop-only, never on GitHub ───────────────────
# This repo ships the website only: backend/ (Render) + frontend/ (Vercel).
# The MyRecon Android app lives in this same working folder for convenience,
# but it is deliberately NOT tracked here. Keep those files — they are the
# only copy — just don't commit them. The frontend pages that advertise the
# app (frontend/app.html, app-ads.txt) are website files and stay tracked.
/app/
/gradle/
/gradlew
/gradlew.bat
/build.gradle.kts
/settings.gradle.kts
/gradle.properties
/play-store/

# local.properties holds this machine's SDK path and must never be committed —
# Android Studio regenerates it per developer.
local.properties
.gradle/
build/
*.apk
*.aab
captures/
.cxx/

# OS
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store

# Logs
*.log

# Scratch scripts
scratch/

# ── Legacy pre-refactor code (NOT deployed; superseded by backend/ + frontend/) ──
# Leading slashes anchor these to the repo root so the real backend/frontend
# copies (e.g. backend/modules, frontend/assets) are NOT ignored.
# You can delete these local files at any time — see README "Legacy cleanup".
/main.py
/web_main.py
/config.py
/vercel.json
/Procfile
/requirements.txt
/requirements-desktop.txt
/gui/
/assets/
/web/
/modules/
/services/
/utils/
/data/

# ── Cryptographic material — never commit ────────────────────────
# `Aran` is a PKCS#12 keystore (contains a private key). If that is the
# Android upload/signing key, publishing it would let anyone sign builds
# impersonating the released app. The .der files are X.509 certificates
# from signing experiments; harmless, but they are build artefacts and do
# not belong in the repo either.
Aran
*.der
*.jks
*.keystore
*.p12
*.pfx
*.pem
!deployment_cert.example.der
